You can start paying off student loans by making a payment plan with your loan lender. You can choose to make either monthly payments or bi-weekly payments. You can also choose to make a lump-sum payment, which is the fastest way to pay off your student loans.

Other ways to help pay off student loans include:

• Refinancing your loans;
• Consolidate your loans;
• Making extra payments;
• Repayment plans;
• Income-based repayment plans;
• Public service loan forgiveness;
• Deferment and forbearance;
• Making a one-time payment;
• Paying off your loans with the proceeds from a settlement, inheritance, or inheritance refund;
• Taking advantage of loan cancellation or discharge programs; and
• Enrolling in a loan assistance program or scholarship.
